Z||000015||RFMike||08-30-99||06:15 PM||||Finally got a response to my e-mail.  This is what 200hp will cost from RSM.<br>Hello!<p>The price on the site includes a long block,  to achieve the 200 HP you will<br>need the following mods:<br>-performance cam $300<br>-1.6 roller rocker arms $225/set<br>-harder valve springs and keepers $190/set<br>-high flow injectors $510/set<br>-high volume fuel pump $195<br>-larger throttle body $249<br>-ignition system & performance coil $400<br>-forged high compression pistons $700/set<p>We also have a bolt-on supercharger (no A/C on the car) that will give you<br>70+ HP at the wheels and we will be posting Dyno results on the site next<br>week.<br>We have been in business for 7 years and build and race Fieros.<br>The engines are built on order and the waiting period is about 4 weeks. The<br>warranty is 1 year on all our engines (unless it is race prepared).<br>Shipping is about $300.00 .<p>Regards<p>Zsolt<br>RS Motorsport
Z||000016||Cooter||08-30-99||07:11 PM||||Let's see if my second grade math can figure this out. . .  price and shipping is $3069. That is not a bargin! For that much, I believe that I would get the v8 Archie kit and pick up a late model z-28 engine and have a little more than 200 horsepower and have spending money left over.
Z||000017||Dale||08-30-99||07:40 PM||||For gas!!!
Z||000018||Shaun41178||08-31-99||01:02 AM||||$490 for a more aggresive cam then stock and the matching springs and retainers?  Please that is such a ripoff.  This cam made out of gold?  They say they build the engines to order so it is not like they are doing any more labor then with a stock rebuild when adding a higher lift cam so why is them so expensive?  I can get a good high lift cam for $99.  Matching springs and retainers for and other small valvetrain bits for anotehr $99.  That is only $200.  Where is the other $290 going?  It shouldn't be going to extra labor.<p>$195 for a larger fuel pump?  You still have to install it.  Talk about an expensive fuel pump.<p>$225 for roller tipped rockers?  You can get comp cams 1.6 rockers designed for the 2.8 from jegs for $130.  So it costs an extra $100 in labor to install these rockers over the stock ones?  whatever.<p>$510 for high flow injectors?  Talk about a rip off.  They are probably using 19# an hour injectors at the most and you can get a set of 8 from jegs for $439 and with the ones from RS you only get 6 and I am unsure if the ones they provide are even 19# an hour.<p>Ignition and coil for $400????  Outrageous!!  I got my crane ignition and coil and accel wires all for $200 from summit.  The ignition and coil were $150.  Its not like they are doing labor to install that ignition casue you are doing it.  Huge profit margin there.<p>Larger throttle body?  I have never heard of one being used on the Fiero.  Exactly where does this larger TB come from or is it a ported factory Fiero TB?  HMMm makes me wonder there.<p>Now if al these prices are canadien which I doubt then I will retract much of what I say about how much they are charging but even if these are canadien prices they are still making a huge profit off of all these parts and giving you the same parts that you can buy from summit or jegs for a lot less.<p>Now the supercharger is what I am interested in.  I too have thought about dropping my a/c since it doesn't work and mounting a supercharger there with a bracket of some sort and a belt from the a/c or a different belt somehow.  I wonder how much this supercharger kit? will cost.  Is it a kit or just a supercharger they provide?<p>The headers in the pic here look just like the ones provided by Chris West of West Coast Fieros if i am not mistaken.<p>I am not trying to say that you should not spend your money with this company cause I am sure they do a good job but they sure do charge a hell of a lot of money for the parts they provide that you could get at much cheaper.  Later, nice day to all.
Z||000019||loafer87gt||08-31-99||05:55 PM||||Yes, these funds are in Canadian dollars. I have talked to Zsolt and Nelson at the RS motorsports (formerly the Fiero Shop)several times and their prices are in line with the other business IMHO. The crew there know their stuff. They were even on the Motor Trend Fiero special (anybody else see that) showing off some of their swaps and work. I am eagerly awaiting picking up one of their supercharger kits. The rotrex unit they are using is actually a belt driven TURBOCHARGER that has had rave reviews from the aftermarket community. It gives you the benfit of a turbo without the lag. Very exciting.
Z||000020||loafer87gt||08-31-99||05:57 PM||||By the way, their price for the Supercharger kit is 3900 Canadian and 600 if you want it installed. Prices are in Canadian funds.<p>
Z||000021||RFMike||08-31-99||09:15 PM||||Sorry, I should have noted that the prices in that e-mail were Canadian dollars.  Life's been hectic; I just dropped in the e-mail.  That's still a lot of cash.
Z||000022||88 Fiero||08-31-99||09:21 PM||||The Rotrex Supercharger that RSM is selling is basically a compressor in which half is from a turbo unit. You can buy the Rotrex itself from EIP Tuning for $1,500.00. Also, the Rotrex size is the same size of the '90's Mustangs alternator...so figure that....{=o)
